{
  "notes": [
    "Every vector is H_FIELDS_V1: preimage = u64_be(len(domain)) || domain || for each field u64_be(len(field)) || field; digest = SHA256(preimage). The digest is SDKRequestEnvelopeV2.body_digest and the bodyDigest of the EIP-712 SDKRequest the user or the session key signs (shared/account_signing_v1.json sdk_request and sdk_request_session).",
    "Field encoding: Hash32 is exactly 32 raw bytes (transport lowercase hex is decoded first), uint64 is 8-byte big-endian, string is UTF-8, type address frames the 20 address bytes decoded from the canonical Bech32 text (both columns are published), and type optional is OPTIONAL_V1: 00 for absent, 01 || FRAME_V1(value) for present.",
    "Projection: SubscribeOutput resume_after_seq follows transport presence, so unset is absent and a set 0 is present 0. GetTaskEvents from_cursor is decimal text on the transport: empty is absent, and otherwise it must be unsigned decimal without leading zeros, at most 2^64-1, and is present (\"0\" is valid); anything else is rejected before hashing. PrepareChallenge local_evidence_digest is bytes: empty is absent, exactly 32 bytes is present, any other length is rejected. The deprecated AckOutputRequest.output_id does not enter the body.",
    "OpenTask: task_hash is recomputed by the verifier from the SignedOrderV2 in OpenTaskHeader.order_envelope (TRUEOPEN_TASK_ORDER_V3) and never taken from the caller, and the order_envelope bytes do not enter the body. payload_ref is not framed either: it must equal \"nexus://sha256/\" || lowercase_hex(input_hash), a transport check shown in the vector's transport column. OpenTaskHeader.signature and signature_scheme must be empty and are not in the body. The base vector opens the order of shared/account_signing_v1.json task_order: task_hash, session_id and order_sequence are that order's taskHash, sessionId and orderSequence, and task_id in the other vectors is TRUEOPEN_TASK_ID_V1(session_id, order_sequence).",
    "tamper: XOR one bit of one framed field. \"byte\" indexes the framed field bytes and may be negative to count from the end; \"bit\" is the bit position inside that byte, 0 being least significant.",
    "replay: \"overrides\" replaces the listed top-level fields with fully typed fields; \"domain\" hashes the unchanged fields under another body domain. SubscribeOutput and GetTaskEvents encode identical field shapes, so their cross-domain rows reproduce each other's base digest: only the domain separates the two methods.",
    "These bodies carry no chain_id. A body is bound to one chain by the EIP-712 SDKRequest that signs it (the chainId typed field and the domain chainId), so cross-chain replay is covered by shared/account_signing_v1.json request_auth_negative_cases, not here. OpenTask is additionally bound through task_hash, whose order commits to chain_id.",
    "The five domains authenticate off-chain requests only: they are not persisted on chain, emit no event and serve no query, and are bound only into the Builder replay record of the request."
  ],
